                <pb facs="0167" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/890: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-09T20:00:00+01:00">December 9, 1942—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6973. I have discussed both with Mr. Eden and Sir Frederick Leith-Ross the
                    substance of the Department’s 6111, December 3, midnight, and they are in full
                    agreement. Mr. Eden is again approaching the Russian Government for its
                    reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
